    "gen": {
     "tool": "edge-tts",
     "voice": "en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural",
     "rate": "+0%",
     "text": "Your phone has a busy life, and most of it happens before you have even had breakfast. It wakes you with messages from your mum, your bank, and three group chats before you even sit up. Then comes the daily routine of checking everything, one small habit at a time, until the battery starts to drop. By midday the battery has fallen to half, and that quiet drop is where the real panic begins. So you do what everyone does, and look for a charger before the afternoon meeting begins at three. You open a shop page to order a spare cable, and wait while the page slowly loads on weak wifi. It feels like a small win, so you scroll a little longer while the rest of the afternoon slips away. Then you buy the cable, press pay, and wait for the little green check to confirm your order today."
    }
   }
  ],
